gned with the\n     subject's `service`, or create a new spec following the\n     naming pattern above. Do not duplicate an existing test.\n  2. Add a single `test('\u003cscenario id\u003e: \u003cshort description\u003e', ...)`\n     whose body translates the subject's `merged_steps` into\n     executable assertions:\n       - `given`  → setup / preconditions\n       - `when`   → the action being tested\n       - `then`   → assertions\n     Use exact step text where reasonable; do not invent\n     behavior beyond what the steps describe.\n  3. The first line of the test name MUST start with the\n     scenario id followed by `: ` so the validation prompt\n     above can find it. Example: `INT-007: ...`.\n  4. Do not modify other tests. Do not edit the registry.\n\n## Your Task\nAnalyze if you have enough context to generate a confident fix.\n\n**If you can generate a confident fix**, output a fix prompt that the\napplier can execute. The applier is allowed to Write new test files\nand Edit existing ones, but ONLY under the four search roots above.\nThe fix MUST:\n- Pick the right tree: `tests/integration/` for `INT-*` scenarios\n  (Playwright Request API, no browser), `tests/e2e/` for `E2E-*`\n  scenarios (Playwright Browser/Page API).\n- Either extend an existing spec file most aligned with the scenario's\n  service or create a new one following the naming pattern\n  `\u003cservice\u003e-*.spec.ts`.\n- Add a single `test('INT-900: \u003cshort description\u003e', ...)`\n  whose body translates the subject's Given / When / Then into\n  executable assertions.\n- Never modify `docs/scenarios.yaml`.\n- Never duplicate an existing test.\n\n=== FILE_START: tmp/2026-08-15-16-02-32-67464/01-INT-900-fix-prompts.md ===\n# Fix Prompt for Scenario INT-900: MCP /mcp endpoint responds 200 to a valid initialize POST\n\n## Target\nApply the change under one of:\n- `tests/integration/\u003cservice\u003e-*.spec.ts`\n- `tests/e2e/\u003cservice\u003e-*.spec.ts`\n- `services/backend/...`